[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3569643581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3569643581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3569643581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UxHA9","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T09:05:34Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T09:05:34Z","body":"I wonder if we should auto detect the view pose based on the composition layer being a child of an `XRCamera3D` node, else positioning in the editor would be a little unintuitive.\r\n\r\nOther than that, worth supporting I guess.\r\n\r\ncc @dsnopek ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3569643581/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3569967689","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3569967689","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3569967689,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7UyWJJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T10:21:31Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T10:21:31Z","body":"Please also fix the style issues before we go ahead and run CI again ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3569967689/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571764297","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3571764297","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3571764297,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U5MxJ","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T16:48:36Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T16:48:36Z","body":"> I wonder if we should auto detect the view pose based on the composition layer being a child of an `XRCamera3D` node, else positioning in the editor would be a little unintuitive.\r\n> \r\n> Other than that, worth supporting I guess.\r\n> \r\n> cc @dsnopek\r\n\r\nJust curious to see if I understand, but if a composition layer is a child of the XR camera, it makes sense to default (or force) to using the `XR_REFERENCE_SPACE_TYPE_VIEW` space which would cause the pose to be relative to the camera and properly reprojected as head locked. This would mean the pose used by the composition layer should be relative to the camera. I don't think it makes sense to use world-locked with something that is a child of a camera. This might remove the need for explicitly specifying world or head locked entirely.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3571764297/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572347130","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3572347130","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3572347130,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U7bD6","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T19:19:11Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T19:19:11Z","body":"> > I wonder if we should auto detect the view pose based on the composition layer being a child of an `XRCamera3D` node, else positioning in the editor would be a little unintuitive.\r\n> > Other than that, worth supporting I guess.\r\n> > cc @dsnopek\r\n> \r\n> Just curious to see if I understand, but if a composition layer is a child of the XR camera, it makes sense to default (or force) to using the `XR_REFERENCE_SPACE_TYPE_VIEW` space which would cause the pose to be relative to the camera and properly reprojected as head locked. This would mean the pose used by the composition layer should be relative to the camera. I don't think it makes sense to use world-locked with something that is a child of a camera. This might remove the need for explicitly specifying world or head locked entirely.\r\n\r\nAt the moment composition layers can only be children of the `XrOrigin3D` node hence why the current approach in the PR. If we do relax that restriction, then yes I agree this would be a good default behavior to have.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572347130/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572611535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3572611535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3572611535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7U8bnP","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-24T20:31:01Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T20:31:01Z","body":"I'm curious about your use case is for eye visibility?\r\n\r\n> I wonder if we should auto detect the view pose based on the composition layer being a child of an `XRCamera3D` node\r\n\r\nI agree that this would be a better \"API\" for this, than exposing it as a property - it would be much more intuitive to Godot developers. As it is now, I think it'll be very confusing, because the position in Godot will be relative to the `XROrigin3D`, but then that will be applied relative to the camera.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3572611535/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573679247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3573679247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3573679247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VAgSP","user":{"login":"stillmant","id":26812793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2ODEyNzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26812793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant","html_url":"https://github.com/stillmant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T03:54:47Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T03:54:47Z","body":"@BastiaanOlij @dsnopek I like the suggestion to automatically switch to View space when a composition layer is a child of the XR camera — I’ll update the PR accordingly!\r\n\r\nRegarding the use case for eye visibility: I’m currently working on a project that streams stereoscopic video from external cameras into head-locked composition layers to provide depth perception to the user. I needed a way to selectively render to each eye's panel or else the panels would cross over into the view of the other eye. I could also see this being useful for asymmetric UI/HUD elements where each eye needs different information. In the past, I’ve worked on XR projects for vision-science research as well, and I believe this feature could support similar experimental setups.\r\n\r\nBefore implementing this, I found this [repo](https://github.com/mgpadalkar/godot_left_right_independent_images) and wanted to build upon that idea so other developers could achieve the same effect more easily, especially since the OpenXR layer structs already support configuring eye visibility.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573679247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573762867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3573762867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3573762867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VA0sz","user":{"login":"stillmant","id":26812793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2ODEyNzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26812793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant","html_url":"https://github.com/stillmant","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stillmant/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T04:44:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T04:44:43Z","body":"@dsnopek As @m4gr3d points out, to support automatically switching between pose spaces based on the layer’s parent, we would need to remove the following configuration warning:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tif (is_visible() && is_inside_tree()) {\r\n\t\tXROrigin3D *origin = Object::cast_to<XROrigin3D>(get_parent());\r\n\t\tif (origin == nullptr) {\r\n\t\t\twarnings.push_back(RTR(\"OpenXR composition layers must have an XROrigin3D node as their parent.\"));\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI’m not completely sure what the broader implications of removing this check would be, but I assume it was added for a good reason. Before making any changes here, I wanted to get your thoughts on whether this warning is still necessary or if it could be relaxed to allow the automatic behavior.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573762867/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573772472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3573772472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3573772472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VA3C4","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T04:50:43Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T04:50:43Z","body":"> Just curious to see if I understand, but if a composition layer is a child of the XR camera, it makes sense to default (or force) to using the `XR_REFERENCE_SPACE_TYPE_VIEW` space which would cause the pose to be relative to the camera and properly reprojected as head locked. This would mean the pose used by the composition layer should be relative to the camera. I don't think it makes sense to use world-locked with something that is a child of a camera. This might remove the need for explicitly specifying world or head locked entirely.\r\n\r\nWe never  use world locked poses with composition layers, they've always been local to the XROrigin3D node, hence that node being the parent.\r\nMaking XRCamera3D an alternative parent, the pose will automatically be correct as again the local pose will be set on the composition layer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573772472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573779316","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3573779316","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3573779316,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VA4t0","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T04:55:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T04:55:05Z","body":"> @dsnopek As @m4gr3d points out, to support automatically switching between pose spaces based on the layer’s parent, we would need to remove the following configuration warning:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> \tif (is_visible() && is_inside_tree()) {\r\n> \t\tXROrigin3D *origin = Object::cast_to<XROrigin3D>(get_parent());\r\n> \t\tif (origin == nullptr) {\r\n> \t\t\twarnings.push_back(RTR(\"OpenXR composition layers must have an XROrigin3D node as their parent.\"));\r\n> \t\t}\r\n> \t}\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> I’m not completely sure what the broader implications of removing this check would be, but I assume it was added for a good reason. Before making any changes here, I wanted to get your thoughts on whether this warning is still necessary or if it could be relaxed to allow the automatic behavior.\r\n\r\nYou wouldn't remove the check, just allow the parent to be either XROrigin3D or XRCamera3D node.\r\nThen check in your enter tree notification whether the parent is XROrigin3D (and use get_play_space), or XRCamera3D (and use get_view_space). I guess for this you could keep `OpenXRCompositionLayer::set_pose_space` but just set the value based on the parent.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3573779316/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3574993303","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3574993303","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3574993303,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VFhGX","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T10:45:24Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T10:45:24Z","body":"> Regarding the use case for eye visibility: I’m currently working on a project that streams stereoscopic video from external cameras into head-locked composition layers to provide depth perception to the user.\r\n\r\nAh, very cool!\r\n\r\n> You wouldn't remove the check, just allow the parent to be either XROrigin3D or XRCamera3D node.\r\n> Then check in your enter tree notification whether the parent is XROrigin3D (and use get_play_space), or XRCamera3D (and use get_view_space).\r\n\r\n:+1:\r\n\r\n> I guess for this you could keep `OpenXRCompositionLayer::set_pose_space` but just set the value based on the parent.\r\n\r\nKeeping the method is fine, but it shouldn't be exposed to users","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3574993303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3575172984","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113096#issuecomment-3575172984","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113096","id":3575172984,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VGM94","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://